		<note type="caution" id="e00040">
			<p>When replacing tires, use the same size originally supplied with the vehicle. Using tires of a different size can damage the related parts or make it work irregularly.</p>
		</note>
		<note type="note" id="e00041">
			<ul id="e00042">
				<li id="e00043">
					<p>We recommend that when replacing tires, use the same originally supplied with the vehicles. If not, that affects driving performance.</p>
				</li>
				<li id="e00044">
					<p>When driving in high altitude grades, it is natural for the atmospheric pressure to decrease. Therefore, please check the tire pressure and add more air when necessary.</p>
					<ul>
						<li id="e00045">
							<p>Additionally, required tire air pressure per km above sea level: 1.5 psi/km</p>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</note>
